# RAG System Development

## Architecture

- `internal/rag/engine.go` — central `Engine` struct with `Troubleshoot()`, `DeepTroubleshoot()`, `SearchDocs()`, `SearchCode()`, `SearchTelcoConfigs()`, `SearchKnownIssues()`, `SearchManifests()`, `CheckFreshness()`
- `internal/rag/store.go` — vector store wrapper around `chromem-go` with `AddDocuments()`, `Search()`, `SearchWithFilter()`, `KeywordSearch()`, `Reset()`
- `internal/rag/mcp/server.go` — MCP server using `mark3labs/mcp-go` v0.56.0, stdio transport. `NewMCPServer(engine)` creates the server, `registerTools()` registers all 8 tools
- `internal/rag/ingest/` — data ingestion pipeline: docs, Go source (via `go/ast`), YAML, markdown, issues
- `internal/rag/embeddings.go` — embedding client (Ollama-compatible HTTP API)

## Vector Store

5 collections in `chromem-go`:

| Collection | Content | Retrieval |
|---|---|---|
| `ocp_docs` | OCP product documentation | Hybrid (BM25 + vector) |
| `operator_code` | Operator Go source code | Hybrid (BM25 + vector) |
| `telco_configs` | Telco-reference validated CRs | Plain vector |
| `known_issues` | Bugs from Bugzilla/Jira | Plain vector, version-aware |
| `manifests` | Operator manifests and CRDs | Plain vector |

## Configuration

`rag-config.yaml` controls: `data_dir`, embedding URL/model, OCP versions, operator repos, retrieval params (top_k, similarity threshold), chunking (size, overlap), ingestion timeouts, secret filtering, freshness metadata.

Override with env vars: `OCP_RAG_DATA_DIR`, `OCP_RAG_EMBEDDING_URL`, `OCP_RAG_EMBEDDING_MODEL`, `OCP_RAG_OCP_VERSION`.

## Adding a New MCP Tool

1. Add `mcp.NewTool("tool_name", mcp.WithDescription(...), mcp.WithString/Array(...))` in `registerTools()` in `internal/rag/mcp/server.go`
2. Implement handler method on `mcpServer` struct
3. Register the handler: `s.srv.AddTool(tool, s.handleNewTool)`
4. Handler signature: `func (s *mcpServer) handleNewTool(ctx context.Context, req mcp.CallToolRequest) (*mcp.CallToolResult, error)`
5. Extract params from `req.Params.Arguments`, call engine methods, return `mcp.NewToolResultText(formatted)`
